540:## SF6c — evidence certification (B01/B02)
542:Before = **SF6b** (`8c5ad361` production sources); after = **SF6c**. Policy id remains `sf6-release-v1`. The SF6 Boolean rule, character inventory, SF5 composer, slot decisions and same-kind capital MOVE exception are unchanged. This section supersedes the original SF6 claim that the old loader never filled a missing score.
544:Policy sha **`6f62925a9a25e956ea7585fd3e07b1043cfd36bea018754c92a7fac86330c406`**, previously `704c47a3ee5b742376b3c73a8dcf0722dc0077f48a839b1109355cf3980f360e`. The binding now covers the score loader, frame-score provenance and all live M2/Clariden runtime builders, as well as the original gate/consumer sources. [Comparison and source binding](SF6c_evidence/comparison.json).
548:- **B01:** `Alignment.confidence` defaults to `None`; omitted/null scores remain missing through load, save, transfer, M2 and Clariden. Legacy runtime copies explicitly retain `scored: false` with missing/unprovenanced provenance. A genuine **0.0 is never positive**. Recogniser absence requires an explicit finite line score **> 0.5**, plus explicit scored observation of the complete saved target window, also **> 0.5**. A finite line average alone cannot authorize absence.
549:- The `ctc-window-score-v1` envelope binds the alignment digest, transcript digest, NFD start/base, image width, target window, valid frame range and score method. Regional confidence is the **minimum** max posterior over **every overlapping frame**, including blanks. New alignments retain actual frame probabilities with their original transcript digest; legacy alignments without them produce **no regional scores**. Object transfers preserve a transferred flag; record transfers are detected by the frame/transcript ownership digest. Transferred spans cannot supply regional observation. The historical shared transfer helper and its old scoring receipt remain unchanged. No saved frame score is invented.
550:- M2 inference and cached-detector replay write those fields. `l1_infer`, `l1e_run` and the held-out L1E builder preserve explicit score/provenance or explicitly mark it unavailable. The historical L1 detector builder existed only in the immutable `artifacts/labelfix_l1e/reference/` snapshot: `scripts/labelfix/clariden/l1_detect.py` is the same builder with only confidence, regional evidence and native width added. Historical references/deploy snapshots remain unchanged. R1 extraction records `line_confidence_missing`, rather than converting missing to zero.
552:- Recognition score, regional provenance and image width are included in the content-bound runtime envelope. No recogniser/detector/reader decisions, alias handling, independent-signal combinations or whole-line HOLD dispatch change.
554:**Floor justification.** `0.5` is the existing saved R1 extraction admissibility cutoff, not a threshold fitted to release outcomes. A strict majority posterior on every observed frame is a conservative lower bound for a positive scored observation; zero and values at the floor HOLD. The saved distribution below places all 666 held-out and all 273 DEV line scores above it, while the broader saved C1 cache has 8/91,469 at or below it. Thus the floor does not manufacture a yield change in these cohorts. These are **line averages**, not regional minimum scores or calibrated absence probabilities: the saved evidence cannot calibrate regional accuracy. Missing regional observations HOLD regardless of a high line mean. Provenance and full-window observation, not the floor alone, repair B01.
556:| Saved score population | n | min | p01 | median | max | at/below 0.5 |
559:| M2 DEV runtime | 273 | 0.519740 | 0.660494 | 0.970228 | 0.995106 | 0 |
564:Every loose runtime/combined/detector-shard and witness-input source on disk was enumerated and hashed; original-label overlays were compared under frozen SF6b and SF6c. DEV filtering occurs **before JSON decoding** for every M2 variant. The locked R0 alignment file was hashed only; locked stratum (ii) decoded/composed **0**. [Per-file audit, distributions, writer paths and status counts](SF6c_evidence/runtime_audit.json).
584:Nine packed code/measurement/mock archives were also checked without extraction or mutation. Four runtime members (64 records each) in the two mock64 archives all omit confidence and regional scores; SF6c adds zero HOLDs. The other seven archives contain no runtime members. Their complete hashes and member results are in the same audit receipt.
595:**New HOLDs:** held-out 0; M2 DEV 0; SF5/L1A/quote witnesses 0; all other audited local runtime sources 0. The main replay changes 28 M2 line/mode check records on 11 unique lines: recogniser absence becomes unavailable because regional scoring was never saved. Every affected line was already HOLD. No mark or release outcome changes. [Exact check changes](SF6c_evidence/check_changes.jsonl), [new-HOLD list](SF6c_evidence/line_changes.jsonl).
